  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 6-layer anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate with air incidence at 0 degrees, unpolarized light. Stack sequence: Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 | Ta2O5 | SiO2 (6 finite layers). Wavelength bands: 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Initialize thicknesses using odd-quarter-wave sequence centered at 250 nm optical thickness, apply ±15 nm perturbation on alternating layers (layers 1, 3, 5: +15 nm; layers 2, 4, 6: -15 nm). Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with step-size multiplier increased to 2.0x baseline. Thickness bounds: 20-400 nm per layer. Objective: minimize weighted average reflectance across both bands, report transmittance into silicon. Exclude previously tested thickness fingerprints: 730f5e44ee20783a, dd540b50edff0d0f, 3171e6f7a12074fe, 8e5fabfdc1c26c60, 3eb0b207ce0785d0, 072959648a8bb226, 26c3ff311537571b, 7a30d797ac6e6808, 63c19962355fa149, 8ddf6036747aaf5f, 4ce1ec7e3b0f4657, 2cb54722fc9896cc. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 6-layer anti-reflection coating on silicon using Ta2O5/SiO2 alternating layers at 0° incidence, unpolarized light, across 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm bands. Minimize average reflectance in both bands while reporting transmittance into silicon. Apply gradient-based thickness optimizer with 2.0× baseline step size, layer bounds 20-400 nm, and ±15 nm absolute thickness uncertainty.",
